ge synopses like `add TITLE [--priority ...]` are written as `Usage: ...` prose instead of code-block lines. That keeps them from being picked up as runnable lines, so the only lines starting with `python -m tasktool` are the working examples.\n\nThe doc also covers a few behaviours I took from reading the code:\n- `--file` must come before the command name.\n- `done` with an unknown id prints an error to stderr and exits 2. Nothing is saved in that case, so valid ids in the same command are not marked.\n- `list --sort due` puts tasks without a due date last.\n- `add` sorts and de-duplicates tags.\n- `export` includes finished tasks.","ttft_ms":2611,"type":"result","duration_ms":63265,"uuid":"c3660ee3-cd32-40bb-bfe0-c2bf0efbdceb","ttft_stream_ms":1842,"time_to_request_ms":725,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":225,"system_prompt":259,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":18,"input_attachments":44,"input_hooks":9,"tool_pool_refresh":4,"init_message":7,"engine_pickup":1,"autocompact":16,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":9,"tool_schema_build":69,"message_normalization":10,"client_creation":30,"request_build":22},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":470,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":178,"time_to_request_major_faults":311,"first_content_frame_ms":1843,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
